# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Apex Print OS — ignore rules
#
#  Build output was tracked from the beginning: 5,519 files, which is 94% of
#  everything git was watching. That buried the ~350 real source changes, made
#  every diff unreviewable, and left a working tree so noisy that genuine
#  uncommitted work was easy to lose.
#
#  Everything below is regenerated by `dotnet build` / `dotnet publish` and does
#  not belong in version control.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── .NET build output ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
[Bb]in/
[Oo]bj/
[Ll]og/
[Ll]ogs/

# ── Publish / packaging ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
publish/
[Pp]ublish/
installer/stage/
installer/output/
*.nupkg
*.snupkg

# ── Visual Studio / Rider / VS Code ──────────────────────────────────────────
.vs/
.idea/
*.user
*.suo
*.userprefs
*.sln.docstates
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json
!.vscode/launch.json
!.vscode/extensions.json

# ── Test + coverage output ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
[Tt]est[Rr]esult*/
coverage*.json
coverage*.xml
coverage*.info
*.coverage
*.trx

# ── Build artefacts that are rebuilt, never edited ───────────────────────────
*.dll
*.exe
*.pdb
*.cache
*.ilk
*.meta
*.obj
*.iobj
*.ipdb
*.tlog

# Keep any third-party binaries that genuinely have to ship with the source.
# Add explicit negations here if such a file exists, e.g.:
# !Tools/SumatraPDF.exe

# ── OS / editor noise ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~

# ── Local secrets — never commit these ───────────────────────────────────────
# The licence signing key must exist only on the server.
*.pfx
*.snk
appsettings.*.local.json
secrets.json
.env
.env.local
